from California now a red hot issue went  to a whole new level this afternoon the  administration is suing that state over  its refusal to cooperate with federal  law over illegal immigration and it's  getting nasty in the Golden State  correspondent Clara Cowan has that story  tonight in Sacramento how dare you  needlessly endanger the lives of our law  enforcement officers to promote a  radical open borders agenda attorney  general jeff sessions threw down the  gauntlet in California  blasting state politicians for their  sanctuary policies and accusing them of  deliberately obstructing federal  immigration law by protecting illegal  immigrants California absolutely appears  to me is using every power it has powers  it doesn't have to frustrate federal law  enforcement president trump showed his  support while speaking to the Latino  coalition earlier today and it's  destroying people's lives so many and  we're going to stop it the Justice  Department is specifically targeting  three California state laws enacted  within the past year one prohibits law  enforcement from asking people about  their immigration status and from  participating in federal enforcement  raids another gives state officials  power over DHS detention facilities and  the third offers protection against  workplace raids this lawsuit marks an  escalation in the ongoing feud between  the Trump administration and immigration  advocates hundreds of whom showed up to  protest chanting shut it down and  blocking the street around the hotel  where sessions delivered his remarks  California's Democratic governor and  attorney general angrily condemned the  DOJ lawsuit as a political stunt  contending their state's sanctuary  policies are on solid legal ground this  is completely unprecedented for the  chief law enforcement of the United  States to come out here and engage in a  political stunt  make wild accusations many of which are  based on outright lies the lawsuit  challenges some of our state laws which  are again fully constitutional in an  exclusive interview with Fox News's  Shannon breeze  sessions vowed to keep fighting somebody  needs to stand up and say no you've gone  too far you cannot do this this is not  reasonable it's radical really and the  Justice Department is reportedly now  looking at other states that have  sanctuary policies they could face legal  action next meantime here in California  both sides are gearing up for a long  legal fight no matter what the district  judge decides the loser will appeal and  this case will likely end up before the  US Supreme Court  Lori Callan thank you in Sacramento
 

